#### Component Documentation

```typescript
/**
 * CourseCard Component
 * 
 * Displays course information in a card format.
 * Used in course grids and search results.
 * 
 * @example
 * ```tsx
 * <CourseCard 
 *   course={courseData}
 *   onEnroll={handleEnroll}
 *   showProgress={true}
 * />
 * ```
 */
interface CourseCardProps {
  /** Course data to display */
  course: Course;
  /** Callback when enroll button is clicked */
  onEnroll: (courseId: string) => void;
  /** Whether to show progress indicator */
  showProgress?: boolean;
}
```

## Security Guidelines

### Secure Coding Practices

#### Input Validation

```typescript
// Always validate and sanitize inputs
@Post()
async createCourse(@Body() createCourseDto: CreateCourseDto) {
  // DTO validation with class-validator
  if (!createCourseDto.title || createCourseDto.title.length > 255) {
    throw new BadRequestException('Invalid title');
  }
  
  // Sanitize HTML content
  const sanitizedDescription = sanitizeHtml(createCourseDto.description);
  
  return this.courseService.create({
    ...createCourseDto,
    description: sanitizedDescription,
  });
}
```

#### Authentication and Authorization

```typescript
// Use proper authentication guards
@Controller('admin')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@ApiBearerAuth()
export class AdminController {
  
  @Get('users')
  @Roles(UserRole.ADMIN, UserRole.SUPER_ADMIN)
  async getUsers() {
    // Only admins can access this endpoint
    return this.userService.findAll();
  }
}
```

#### Data Protection

```typescript
// Never expose sensitive data
@Injectable()
export class UserService {
  async getUserProfile(userId: string): Promise<Partial<User>> {
    const user = await this.userRepository.findOne({ where: { id: userId } });
    
    // Return only safe fields
    const { password, ...safeUser } = user;
    return safeUser;
  }
}
```

### Security Testing

```typescript
// Test for security vulnerabilities
describe('Security Tests', () => {
  it('should prevent SQL injection', async () => {
    const maliciousInput = "'; DROP TABLE users; --";
    
    await request(app.getHttpServer())
      .post('/api/courses')
      .send({ title: maliciousInput })
      .expect(400);
  });

  it('should sanitize HTML content', async () => {
    const htmlInput = '<script>alert("xss")</script>';
    
    const result = await courseService.create({
      title: 'Test Course',
      description: htmlInput,
    });

    expect(result.description).not.toContain('<script>');
  });
});
```

## Review Process

### Code Review Checklist

#### Functional Review

```markdown
✅ Functionality works as expected
✅ Edge cases handled properly
✅ Error handling implemented
✅ Performance considerations addressed
✅ Security vulnerabilities checked
```

#### Code Quality Review

```markdown
✅ Code follows style guidelines
✅ TypeScript types are correct
✅ Variable and function names are descriptive
✅ Code is well-organized and readable
✅ No duplicated code
```

#### Testing Review

```markdown
✅ Tests cover new functionality
✅ Tests are well-written and maintainable
✅ Edge cases are tested
✅ Integration tests included when needed
✅ Test coverage meets requirements
```

### Review Guidelines

#### For Reviewers

1. **Be constructive**: Provide helpful, specific feedback
2. **Be thorough**: Check security, performance, and maintainability
3. **Be respectful**: Maintain professional communication
4. **Be timely**: Review within 48 hours

#### For Contributors

1. **Respond promptly**: Address feedback quickly
2. **Explain decisions**: Provide rationale for changes
3. **Be open to feedback**: Consider all suggestions
4. **Update documentation**: Keep docs in sync with code

## Community Guidelines

### Code of Conduct

#### Our Pledge

We are committed to providing a welcoming and inclusive environment for all contributors, regardless of:

- Experience level
- Gender identity and expression
- Sexual orientation
- Disability
- Personal appearance
- Body size
- Race, ethnicity, age, religion, or nationality

#### Expected Behavior

```markdown
✅ Use welcoming and inclusive language
✅ Be respectful of different viewpoints and experiences
✅ Gracefully accept constructive criticism
✅ Focus on what is best for the community
✅ Show empathy towards other community members
```

#### Unacceptable Behavior

```markdown
❌ Harassment, trolling, or inappropriate behavior
❌ Personal attacks or political discussions
❌ Publishing private information
❌ Any other conduct which could reasonably be considered inappropriate
```

### Communication Guidelines

#### GitHub Issues

```markdown
